wh40k-footfall-cargo-marker-desc = Persistent scene source. Rotate the arrow before map initialization; place seated actors on the tile of a free chair or bench.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-name = Cargo visitor with a ticket
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-desc = A resident awaiting their order, occasionally recounting the queue numbers.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-marker = Marker: Cargo visitor with a ticket
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-line-1 = I took a ticket for one crate. Now I'm wondering if I need another to lift it.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-line-2 = They promised delivery before the end of the shift. We haven't established which shift.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-line-3 = I ordered tools. Sit here much longer and I'll receive them as a family heirloom.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentone-line-4 = Hest says the cargo is on its way. Judging by the time, it's coming on foot.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-name = Cargo visitor awaiting boots
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-desc = A resident waiting for new boots. The old pair still works, but has begun lodging complaints.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-marker = Marker: Cargo visitor awaiting boots
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-line-1 = Ordered boots a size larger. While I wait, the old ones have become a size smaller.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-line-2 = If they lost my boots, tell me where. At least I'll know where to walk barefoot.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-line-3 = Everyone else's cargo is fragile. Mine's my patience. Somehow it wasn't packed.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidenttwo-line-4 = I'm sitting quietly. One sole of my old boots has started its own trade in air.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-name = Cargo visitor with a long manifest
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-desc = A resident waiting for a small order with an unexpectedly long list of clarifications.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-marker = Marker: Cargo visitor with a long manifest
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-line-1 = It's a small order: three things. Seven clarifications so far. Soon the paperwork will need its own crate.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-line-2 = They asked me to wait a minute. Being polite, I didn't ask which calendar they use.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-line-3 = Last time they mixed up the boxes. Now I read the small print on the tape before signing.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowaitingresidentthree-line-4 = My neighbour wants boots; I want a filter. Another delay and we'll start a support group here.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-name = Cargo dispatch worker
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-desc = A worker checking manifests and locating requested goods in the warehouse.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-marker = Marker: Cargo dispatch worker
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-line-1 = Your item is on the list. Now to find somewhere it exists outside the list.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-line-2 = Whoever labelled a crate miscellaneous, come here. Everything's miscellaneous; that isn't an address.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-line-3 = I remember shelf numbers. Faces, less well. You can introduce yourself as rack three.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargodispatchworker-line-4 = Hest's manifests are in order. The warehouse is too; we're just still looking for that order.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-name = Cargo warehouse sorter
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-desc = A worker sorting goods by category and disputing someone else's labelling system.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-marker = Marker: Cargo warehouse sorter
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-line-1 = Tools left, supplies right. Mystery parts go wherever the person who labelled them will look.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-line-2 = I sorted alphabetically. My colleague sorted by weight. Now the warehouse runs on mood.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-line-3 = When the manifest says about ten, I'm still the one counting.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousesorter-line-4 = That crate has returned to the same shelf three times. Apparently it considers it home.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-name = Cargo warehouse packer
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-desc = A worker preparing shipments. Their orange hard hat stands out even among the crates.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-marker = Marker: Cargo warehouse packer
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-line-1 = Checked the fragile label. Now to find a loader who can read while walking.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-line-2 = Packing air is free. Until Hest invents a separate manifest for it.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-line-3 = Wrapped it twice, labelled it three times. Now to convince the crate it's ready to travel.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargowarehousepacker-line-4 = Someone asked for secure packing. It's so secure that now I'm looking for the opening myself.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-name = Miner back from a sortie
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-desc = A miner in Lithos gear, back with commissioned ore and still holding a pickaxe.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-marker = Marker: Miner back from a sortie
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-line-1 = Brought the commissioned ore. The rock didn't argue about the price. That's one reason I like this job.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-line-2 = Space is quiet. Here they asked why the ore was so heavy before I got through the door.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-line-3 = They ordered ore; dust was included. Anyone wanting only dust can wait until I take my boots off.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-cargoreturningminer-line-4 = Checked my fastenings twice, the manifest once. Hest thinks that's the wrong balance.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-name = Engineer struggling with a solder joint
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-desc = An engineer in a separate workshop, ten hours into one soldering job. Their expression is more convincing than the result.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-marker = Marker: Engineer struggling with a solder joint
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-1 = Ten hours trying to solder plus to minus. The circuit objects, the supervisor is busy, and now it's a matter of principle.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-2 = Found plus, found minus. Lost my confidence somewhere between them.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-3 = First I thought I needed more solder. Now I suspect the idea itself is the surplus part.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-4 = If anyone asks, work is progressing. Very slowly, and mostly in circles.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-5 = Labelled the wires in hour nine. In hour ten, discovered the labels were wrong. Nice handwriting, though.
wh40k-footfall-cargo-workshopsolderingengineer-line-6 = I don't work in cargo. At least they know where to send something that didn't work out.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-hestvarn-pickup-choice = How does cargo dispatch work?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-hestvarn-pickup-reply = First we establish what arrived and who it's for. The worker at the window locates the item; the warehouse checks count and packing. An unlabelled crate calls for an inspection, not a gift to the first passerby. My commissions are separate: take work through the log, read the terms, and bring the required cargo to me. Waiting for someone else's order doesn't complete a contract.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-hestvarn-mining-choice = How do you work with miners?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-hestvarn-mining-reply = The salvage centre handles material from sorties: ore needs sorting, processing, and checking against the commission. The pickaxe goes back to the miner; unexpected finds need a separate discussion. Garrick Morn handles specialised mining contracts; I handle supplies and deliveries. If a commission asks for goods, a story about a shattered asteroid won't replace them. Even a good story.

